00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:30.699
This woman you see on the screen is Meng Wanzhou,
Vice President of Huawei.

00:00:30.699 --> 00:00:33.880
The Canadian police arrested her at the end
of 2018.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:43.460
The main reason was because of alleged violations
of America’s sanctions on Iran.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.530
But there’s more to the story.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:51.460
The Trump administration believes China is
using their technology to spy on American

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.460
citizens.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:57.800
But… is this just Donald Trump’s obsession
or are there legitimate reasons to be scared

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:05.129
of China?

00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:11.570
You see… whenever we talk about the military,
we always talk about air, sea and land…

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:14.709
nowadays we should add another field: technology.

00:01:14.709 --> 00:01:26.039
Chips, cameras, drones and all kinds of innovations
that have revolutionized modern warfare.

00:01:26.039 --> 00:01:31.899
As we told you in our previous videos, China
is facing an existential threat and therefore

00:01:31.899 --> 00:01:34.149
it needs to expand the military.

00:01:34.149 --> 00:01:38.229
This is why they created what has been called
the String of Pearls strategy.

00:01:38.229 --> 00:01:43.319
This is a set of ports that can double as
military bases that would go from the South

00:01:43.319 --> 00:01:44.729
China Sea to Africa.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:49.950
And, in another video, we told you about what
we like to call sugar daddy diplomacy.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:57.979
But still, there is something important China
is missing for their military expansion: technology.

00:01:57.979 --> 00:02:02.999
And, catching up with the West in this field
is not easy.

00:02:02.999 --> 00:02:07.219
And again, Xi Jimping is showing his lateral
thinking on this issue…

00:02:07.219 --> 00:02:08.450
How?

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:14.150
We’ll tell you in this video.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.280
China.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:25.150
A country famous for making cheap copies of
anything that you can imagine, like these

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:29.099
copyrights violating ”LEPIN” bricks with
the STAR…

00:02:29.099 --> 00:02:32.739
WNRS logo on them…

00:02:32.739 --> 00:02:39.219
But make no mistake…

00:02:39.219 --> 00:02:43.459
China’s technological prowess goes way beyond
that.

00:02:43.459 --> 00:02:49.469
In 2015 China’s government unveiled “Made
in China 2025”, a ten-year plan to update

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:54.650
the state’s manufacturing base by rapidly
developing ten high-tech industries.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:59.049
Chief among these are electric cars and other
new energy vehicles, next-generation information

00:02:59.049 --> 00:03:05.840
technology and telecommunications, and, last
but not least, advanced robotics and artificial

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:06.959
intelligence.

00:03:06.959 --> 00:03:12.150
These sectors are central to the so-called
fourth industrial revolution, which is the

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:15.049
new buzzword to use when you want to look
smarter.

00:03:15.049 --> 00:03:19.810
Soon there won’t be a single talk show or
political debate that isn’t talking about

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:21.450
it so… pay attention.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:26.670
The fourth industrial revolution refers to
the integration of big data and cloud computing

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:30.920
into global manufacturing supply chains.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:40.230
’Made in China 2025’: is Beijing’s plan
for hi-tech dominance as big a threat as the

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.689
West thinks it is?

00:03:41.689 --> 00:03:44.599
The plan is to reduce the dependence on foreign
technology.

00:03:44.599 --> 00:03:48.810
Yes, it is true, most of the mobile phones
you can buy are assembled in China.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:53.069
But the majority of the high tech components,
the cameras, the high end microchips… all

00:03:53.069 --> 00:03:56.829
of that, is made in countries like America,
Germany or Japan.

00:03:56.829 --> 00:04:00.829
So far China doesn’t have the technology
to produce those components.

00:04:00.829 --> 00:04:06.879
And that’s why this desire to become a tech
superpower is part of the so called Chinese

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:08.529
dream.

00:04:08.529 --> 00:04:14.709
“The Chinese dream is closely linked with
the dreams of people in other countries ... China’s

00:04:14.709 --> 00:04:18.660
development is facilitated by the development
of the world, and it will bring about the

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:23.500
greater impetus and opportunities for the
common progress of all countries” – President

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:26.590
Xi Jinping, October 22nd, 2015

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:29.130
And now, China is trying to make another Silicon
Valley.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:33.870
The city of Nanjing, for example, is currently
developing a research park to foster China’s

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.310
next generation of tech giants.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:40.669
We’re talking about an area as big as SEATTLE
,housing dozens of high-profile startups and

00:04:40.669 --> 00:04:41.669
companies.

00:04:41.669 --> 00:04:42.699
And that’s just one big city.

00:04:42.699 --> 00:04:46.740
It’s worth noting that this comes with the
support of the Chinese government.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:50.319
And this support comes with heavy regulations.

00:04:50.319 --> 00:04:55.230
Businesses must meet certain criteria to qualify
for tax relief and other support.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.730
And there’s even more here…

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:01.949
Besides providing subsidies and setting targets,
how does China intend to achieve its goals?

00:05:01.949 --> 00:05:06.810
By investing or, directly buying American
and European startups.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:10.690
Chinese companies, both private and state-backed,
have been encouraged to invest in foreign

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:13.620
companies in order to gain access to advanced
technology.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:19.629
In 2016 alone, the value of Chinese acquisitions
in the United States amounted to over $45

00:05:19.629 --> 00:05:20.629
billion.

00:05:20.629 --> 00:05:22.110
And the same goes for in Europe.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:24.819
OK, I know what you’re thinking… so what?

00:05:24.819 --> 00:05:27.630
What’s the problem if China wants to invest
in other countries?

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:32.870
Well, the problem is that many of those investments
might be a strategy to steal technology from

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:34.430
Europe and America.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.569
And, believe me, I’m not making this up.

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:37.660
Want an example?

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:38.660
Here it is!

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:39.720
You know those OREO cookies?

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:43.100
Well… that sweet cream they have in the
middle is so pearly White because they use

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:45.440
a special Chemical component.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:50.130
Something based on Titanium dioxide that requires
rocket science to produce.

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:55.531
The patent to produce this belongs to a company
called DUPONT and it’s as secret as the

00:05:55.531 --> 00:05:57.270
Coca Cola formula.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:02.599
So one day, a Chinese spy called Walter LIEW
stole this formula.

00:06:02.599 --> 00:06:09.830
Years later, a Chinese factory was mass producing
this White tint.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.550
And that’s just an example!

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:16.630
Of course, in the Oreo case, the patent holders
could act and file a lawsuit against the spies.

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:21.060
But… what would happen if, instead of being
a spy, this Walter LIEW guy had been the main

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:22.610
shareholder of the company?

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:26.310
In this case, he would have access to the
company’s secrets without a problem.

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:28.270
And I know what you’re thinking…

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:29.580
Who cares about cookies?

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.590
Well… cookies aren’t important, you’re
right.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:36.350
But… what if, instead of white cream, we
were talking about military technology?

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:38.020
Then we could have a problem.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:43.110
And believe me, China would LOVE to get military
secrets from European and American companies.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:46.940
And you might wonder… is this as bad as
some politicians are making it out to be?

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:51.409
Or is this just another chapter in the trade
war with China?

00:06:51.409 --> 00:06:54.750
Today we’re going to answer to all of these
questions but, before we do, let’s take

00:06:54.750 --> 00:07:00.659
a look back at the history.

00:07:00.659 --> 00:07:02.960
MORE MONEY AND EVEN MORE DEALS

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:07.050
When it comes to investing in technology,
Americans already have a huge funding market.

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:08.680
Want to create a start up?

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:13.430
Just in California you’ll find lots of VC
funds competing to make the best deal with

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:14.430
you.

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:16.790
But the European Union is more of a virgin
territory.

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:21.229
And this is why the European Union became
the favorite destination for Chinese investors.

00:07:21.229 --> 00:07:24.970
According to several studies published by
the Mercator Institute for China Studies,

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:32.650
the foreign direct investment or FDI in the
EU totaled more than €35 billion in 2016,

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:36.770
with a 77% increase from the previous year.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:45.930
And Germany was the largest recipient, accounting
for 31% of all that money.

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:48.620
Chinese investment in Europe is increasing.

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:53.979
The region accounted for a quarter of China’s
FDI outflows in 2017

00:07:53.979 --> 00:07:58.800
Chinese investors have always showed a strong
predilection for tech and advanced manufacturing

00:07:58.800 --> 00:07:59.800
assets.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:04.349
Some of the big deals made were the acquisition
of a German robotics company for €4.4 billion

00:08:04.349 --> 00:08:09.189
and the €6.7 billion acquisition of Finnish
gaming firm Supercell.

00:08:09.189 --> 00:08:13.379
And those are just the bigger ones… just
think about what €35 billion could do.

00:08:13.379 --> 00:08:19.379
In the last couple years China began refocusing
on the Big Three European economies: Germany,

00:08:19.379 --> 00:08:21.189
the UK and France.

00:08:21.189 --> 00:08:24.650
Those three together accounted for 59% of
their total investment.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:28.449
I know, I know, we’re throwing a lot of
numbers your way.

00:08:28.449 --> 00:08:40.040
But it’s very important in order to understand
the magnitude of this phenomenon.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:44.020
This is a database launched in order to track
and cover China’s global investments.

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:49.390
The database covers China’s global outbound
investments since 2005 and it’s now hosted

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:51.460
by the American Enterprise Institute.

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:56.210
The dataset is publicly available and also
includes construction contracts and transactions

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:58.960
that were never completed.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:02.770
How China is buying its way into Europe.

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:07.450
Bloomberg got to work and provided us with
some pretty intense numbers: just in the past

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:13.210
10 years China has bought or invested in assets
amounting to at least $318 billion.

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:17.850
Most of this money went to businesses but
some also went to infrastructure: just in

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:21.700
the city of London, Chinese investors purchased
a dozen office towers.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:25.480
Knowing who is buying all these businesses
and buildings in Europe is important in order

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:32.240
to try and understand how this kind of activity
fits into China’s foreign policy.

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:37.920
Keeping in mind that the line between state
and private is pretty blurry in China, it’s

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:43.390
worth noting that at least 63% of the total
investments comes from state-backed companies

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:44.390
or investment funds.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:45.390
In other words…

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:49.110
It is China’s government that’s investing
in technological firms.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.930
But why?

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:54.980
Is this all about making money or… perhaps
there’s something more.

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:57.330
We’ll see right now.

00:09:57.330 --> 00:10:00.670
DON’T TOUCH MY TECH!

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:05.490
Even though Silicon Valley comes to mind whenever
someone talks about tech, we shouldn’t overlook

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:06.790
European tech giants.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:10.150
Spotify, for example, is the most valuable
streaming service on the planet.

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:13.620
The company has been valued at around $16
billion.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:15.310
And guess where they come from?

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:16.310
Exactly!

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:17.310
Sweden!

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:19.150
But we’re not here to talk about civil technology.

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:21.600
We’re here to talk about military ones.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:27.380
And here, Europe has a lot to offer.

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:31.480
For example, one of the biggest weapon manufacturers
is the Airbus Group.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:38.570
This French corporation designs, manufactures
and sells civil and military aerospace products

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:44.720
worldwide and in 2017 had a reported revenue
of €67 million.

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:49.410
Military tech is a very sensitive strategic
topic and usually, it’s kept very well hidden.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:53.440
But, if you invest in a company, you can access
their databases and their secrets.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:58.960
At the end of the day, you are one of the
owners!

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:01.740
And this is, exactly, what happened to HUMMER.

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:04.510
Hummers are these armored cars you see on
the screen.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:11.590
The American army has been using them for
decades.

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:16.300
In the year 2008, the company who manufactured
them, a subsidiary of General Motors, was

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:17.920
at the edge of collapse.

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:20.460
And this is when a Chinese company came to
the rescue.

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:24.940
In their first negotiations, they asked for
a couple of cars so they could examine them.

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:27.120
Which is normal, right?

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:30.440
You don’t invest half a billion dollars
in a company without knowing exactly what

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:31.440
they do.

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:33.300
So Hummer gave them those cars.

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:37.270
Then, the White House, with Obama as president,
vetoed the Chinese acquisition.

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:38.270
Why?

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:43.730
Well, they didn’t want to sell a military
company to another country, of course.

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:48.240
Nevertheless, those Chinese investors had
already gotten what they wanted: the cars.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.890
So what did they do with them?

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:52.010
Something called REVERSE ENGINEERING.

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:56.840
They basically took all the pieces apart and
learned how to build their own hummers from

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:57.840
the scratch.

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:03.740
Since then, THESE are the Chinese army’s
brand new armoured cars.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:09.140
Yes, they are almost exactly the same as the
American hummers.

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:11.010
And this is just an example.

00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:12.760
There are many, many more.

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:19.670
So in Europe, they learned the lesson… and
are determined to not repeat the same mistakes.

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:24.380
Is Europe Finally Pushing Back On Chinese
Investments?

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:28.710
And that’s why Europe’s three major powers,
Germany, France, and the U.K., have all recently

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:32.200
taken steps to closely scrutinize Chinese
investments.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:33.720
They have reasons to be afraid.

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:38.650
For example, Germany produces some state of
the art tanks, the so called LEOPARDS.

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:43.120
Well… according to many experts, the new
Chinese tanks have identical motors.

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:48.470
This is why Germany recently vetoed the Chinese
attempt to invest $2 billion in robotics in

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:55.230
their country, citing national security concerns.

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:58.800
The government is also working on a proposal
that would strengthen government vetting of

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:00.430
acquisitions by foreigners

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:01.950
And the same goes in France.

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:06.750
French lawmakers passed a legislation, as
early as 2003, that also allows the government

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:09.110
to scrutinize and veto foreign investments.

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:13.100
Since them, they have added more regulations
for companies in the big data, artificial

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:16.680
intelligence and robotics industries.

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:23.380
“France is open to long-term investment
from China, but not looting” French Finance

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:25.000
Minister Bruno Le Marie.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:28.620
And, you know, anytime France and Germany
agree on something, it’s just a matter of

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:32.260
time before the European Union follows suit.

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:37.760
The agreed package will ensure that the EU
and its Member States are equipped to protect

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:43.520
their “essential interests” while remaining
“one of the most open investment regimes”

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:44.520
in the world.

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:46.190
And this is when the complicated part starts.

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:51.460
Because the line that separates those “essential
interests” and the not so special is…

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:53.140
extremely blurry.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:57.330
You see, we all agree that a company that
manufactures tanks is a weapon manufacturer

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:59.940
and that we want to protect it.

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:00.950
No debate there.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:01.950
But…

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:06.250
What happens with the company that produces
the microchip that controls the computer on

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:07.250
board?

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:11.840
That might be an IT company that works with
lots of clients, aside from the military one.

00:14:11.840 --> 00:14:22.300
In fact, AIRBUS itself has a civil division
and they produce commercial airliners…

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:23.550
Should we protect them too?

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:27.970
In other words… those “essential interests”
can become a trojan horse for all kinds of

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:31.830
protectionist and, arguably, financially xenophobic
measures.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:38.780
And, believe me, the risk on this matter is
also real…

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:45.100
Emmanuel Macron promises to stop foreign investors
buying up French farms after China land grab

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:46.430
Yes, you heard that right!

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:49.700
How on earth is farming related to the military?

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:51.740
Hmm… hard to understand, right?

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:55.130
But the truth is, French farmers don’t like
the Chinese.

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:58.350
And Macron has elections to win in the future.

00:14:58.350 --> 00:15:00.390
And the same goes for the United Kingdom.

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:04.560
For example, in the year 2016, the British
government vetoed a Chinese investment in

00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:05.860
a nuclear power plant.

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:10.200
Was that a strategic decision or straight
forward protectionism?

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:15.880
Well… it’s hard to tell!

00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:18.610
And I know--- I know what many of you might
me thinking!

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:20.520
Fuck the Chinese! right?

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:23.390
Well… the truth is… we need that Money!

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:24.820
Remember that story about Hummer?

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:34.180
So guess what happened right after the White
House vetoed the Chinese aquisition…

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:37.280
General Motors to Close Hummer After Sale
Fails

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:41.750
From one day to the next… , almost 3000
people lost their jobs.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:45.100
And what about those 35 billion euros for
European startups?

00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:49.160
On a previous VisualPolitik video, we told
you the story behind Silicon Valley and how

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:51.910
Europe was unable to attract Venture Capital
funds.

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:57.150
It’s a fact: Brussels, Berlin and Paris
are going crazy trying to find entrepreneurs.

00:15:57.150 --> 00:16:00.500
Europe wants to lead that so-called Fourth
Industrial Revolution.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:04.570
But you don’t do that with grants and subsidies
alone.

00:16:04.570 --> 00:16:08.250
You need Venture Capitalists and private investors
of all kinds.

